{"repositoryId":1296957972,"availability":"available","full":"grognard-xml/grognard","name":"grognard","description":"An XML editor forked from LEAF-Writer for East Asian historical documents","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-10T22:48:21Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:51:34Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://grognard-xml.github.io/grognard/","topics":[],"demo":"https://grognard-xml.github.io/grognard/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:47.674Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:47.674Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:47.674Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:47.674Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Grognard is a desktop XML markup editor forked from the in-browser tool LEAF-Writer, part of The Linked Editing Academic Framework (LEAF) tool suite. LEAF-Writer is an enhancement of the CWRC-Writer developed by the Canadian Writing Research Collaboratory (CWRC), and was developed alongside the Named Entity Recognition Vetting Environment (NERVE). The project website is github.com/grognard-xml/grognard. Grognard wraps the web app in Electron for offline, individual desktop use and includes workflow changes aimed particularly at local editing and East Asian documents.","Grognard is a WYSIWYG XML editor built around a heavily customized TinyMCE core (from LEAF-Writer), packaged as an Electron desktop app. This README focuses on the desktop fork. Planning notes and architecture docs live under docs/.","Grognard is the desktop, offline-first fork of LEAF-Writer. The current build already supports:"],"features":["Opening a local project folder and bootstrapping its schema and project metadata.","Browsing XML files in a project tree, with multiple tabs in one window.","Saving edits back to disk, including the new-file and Save As flow for untitled documents.","Editing in both visual and source mode